Z||000012||artherd||09-27-2001||04:07 AM||||Nah, it's time to get a bigger proxy box/farm  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> (Or at least click some more procs and RAM into the old one.)<P>I think I wouldn't at all mind<P>Hey Cliff, ever thought about basing the Fourm off an SQL db? (not sure how hard that is with UBB, would we basically junk everything, or can UBB now hook into a db?)<P>Not that the Fourm isn't basically the fastest web board I've used in recent memory or anything ;o)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jake_Dragon:<BR><B>I work in the IS department, when the Proxy / web host gets slow its time to clear the cache and reboot   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000013||grinthock||09-28-2001||07:28 AM||||He could base it on MYSQL.  Slashdot.org uses a HTTP server farm talking to a MYSQL server.  Basically what happens is a request for the WWW page comes into the webserver then it sends the SQL requests to a master server.  Speeds it up because you can have a server farm of the HTTP servers all requestings stuff from the MYSQL box.  You could even put a server here in N/A to help speed it up even more and that N/A server could send it's SQL req to the MYSQL in NL<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif">  </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.<p>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 09-28-2001).]||||reg||1
